zd5 = z3x + CAT_FRONT 8 (new switch, zfr's: `zfr` is a zl0 snapshot with the switch; its Baby.java hunks applied to a zc9 snapshot with RUSH_FROM put back to 4) + CASH_READ_LEFT 6000. Cfg.java and Baby.java are the only files that differ from z3x: the CAT_FRONT line and Baby.catFront (ledgered, G.settle K 20), CASH_READ_LEFT and z7u's budget read in cashTick's squeak loop.
Lever: a gatherer flees a cat in view within GATHER_CAT_DIST (dist2 20 from its 2x2 centre) only when the cat can sense it now or after one 45-degree turn of its ATTACK sweep (the 180-degree cone about its facing or about the facing rotated toward its chirality, from the centre), or when within dist2 8 of the centre. Engine (InternalRobot): an exploring cat follows its waypoints and attacks only what blocks its next footprint; an attacking cat targets rats it senses (vision 17, 180 degrees), pounces up to dist2 13 from its centre, and rotates 45 degrees a turn when it finds nothing to do. A gatherer behind a cat keeps working instead of running.
Evidence: local z3x games (cq80-cq88, indicator mv codes), the 'c' (cat flee) share of gatherer turns is 0.7% overall but 11.1% on 5t4rv4t10n, 10.5% mincemeat, 7.8% canyoudig (Xzibit A/B are set-2 anchor losses), 4.1% whatsthecatdoin, 3.8% averyfineline. Replica starved losses: gatherers lost 25 rats / 4,922 cheese to cats, only 1,470 of it on rats that had seen the cat (TRAINING_LOG 2026-11-01, u4e field games), so the flee is rarely what saves them.
